{%- comment -%}
  /pages/editor — the Create/upload/editor/design tool as its own
  bookmarkable, shareable URL, separate from the homepage.

  Deliberately reuses the exact same 'memobrick-site' section the
  homepage renders, rather than extracting the upload/editor/design
  markup into a new section. That markup is the most tightly-coupled part
  of the whole theme — canvas processing, face detection, drag handlers,
  the size picker, the wall visualiser — all sharing one JS state machine
  (the S object, showView(), renderIfNeeded()) with dozens of specific
  element ids referenced across ~900 lines. Physically splitting that
  apart without a live Shopify environment to test against risks
  breaking the actual revenue-generating tool over a URL preference.

  Instead: window.MB_LANDING_VIEW below tells the shared boot script
  (assets/memobrick.js) to open on the "upload" view by default here,
  instead of "home". Every marketing CTA that used to jump to the
  in-page upload view now links to this URL as a real navigation
  instead, so it's a genuine separate page/URL from the visitor's
  perspective — same tool, same tested code, new address.

  Tradeoff, stated plainly: both this page and the homepage still ship
  the same full section markup (marketing sections + the tool), just
  defaulting to a different starting view — this does not reduce either
  page's weight. A true code-level split remains a real future option if
  that matters more than the risk of doing it without live testing.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>window.MB_LANDING_VIEW = "upload";</script>
{% section 'memobrick-site' %}
<script src="{{ 'memobrick-size-zoom.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
